   128	
   129	**Reviewer: Codex.** The reviewer supports the rulings at their stated scope,
   130	with the following reservations about their subsequent use. The author
   131	described these reservations as reasonable and requested that they be noted.
   132	They preserve limitations already discussed; they do not reverse the ACCEPT
   133	decisions or create additional exit prerequisites.
   134	
   135	- **R10 and R21:** accepting the classifier result and incomplete
   136	  correspondence sheet must not be represented as establishing correct
   137	  composition of the models or preservation of their guarantees by the
   138	  implementation. The assurance gap remains real.
   139	- **R18:** accepting the completed strict results must not close the capstone
   140	  or silently resolve its deferred questions.
   141	- **R6:** the operational boundary must follow actual dependencies and
   142	  credentials, including GCP's role. Use of another provider does not by
   143	  itself establish independence.
   144	
