docs/V1-DERIVATION-DRAFT.md:61:| C5 | **Time.** The framed bytes existed no later than T, the earliest verified attestation **in the presented OTS proof**. The authenticated anchor and k-th confirmation header timestamps satisfy the registered three-conjunct predicate. This is presentation-sensitive: a different presentation of the same receipt can select a different T. | No lower bound, no priority (A7 §A7.4). Header timestamps are chain-time proxies (skew, non-monotonic; A2.1). k = 6 assumes forging six mainnet blocks costs more than a receipt is worth, and canonical history at the pinned headers. A reorganization deeper than k is a residual. |
docs/V1-DERIVATION-DRAFT.md:65:**V1's fixed profile,** `tessera-v1-strict`, carried inside the signed bytes:
docs/V1-DERIVATION-DRAFT.md:67:- **Encoding.** `formal/p8/ENCODING-V1.md`: RFC 8785 under the **value-preserving number rule** (accept a number exactly when RFC 8785's canonical form preserves its value; this replaces the registered literal rule, see A9.8), in tag-headed frames with u16 version and u32 length. The two signer frames share the common bytes and differ only in the fingerprint slot. KMS key: `sha256` of the SPKI. GPG key: `sha256` of the OpenPGP key packet (no SHA-1). DNS key publication: TXT at `_tessera-v1.<D>`. P8 prose proof: `formal/p8/PROOF.md`; vectors with two agreeing decoders in `formal/p8/vectors/`.
