docs/V1-DERIVATION-DRAFT.md:280:3. **Q3. Revocation:** (a) `NOT_EVALUATED`, as in A9.4; or (b) at ship time (after k = 6, so after `anchor_time`), the issuer embeds a git-channel statement, OTS-anchored, that no revocation of K was effective at or before ship time. (b) turns one conjunct into an evaluated, issuer-asserted check. It stops a thief who holds K but not the repository key from minting receipts that pass after a revocation. It does not catch a revocation decided later with a backdated effective time. It costs about 1.5 owner-days before 30 Oct and adds one more anchoring cycle, a few hours, to every receipt's latency. *Owner recommends (a):* the narrowed claim already meets the success definition, and (b) can be added later in its own profile.
