docs/implementation-spec.md:1423:**R-5.49** A party needing portable attribution, evaluation-time evidence, or tamper-evident transport may separately attest the complete base result as a distinct typed wrapper. Its bounded claim is that an identified evaluator assessed an identified bundle under an identified environment and obtained the enclosed result. It neither changes that result nor elevates envelope validity into payload truth; signer authority, key lifecycle and report policy belong to that separate attestation profile and are not smuggled into the base verifier contract. [REGISTERED A3 §A3.8, docs/phase-0-prereg-amendment-3.md:712-720]
