docs/reviews/v1-derivation/CODEX-REVIEW.md:230:**Exact fix:** Publish a dependency schedule with parallelizable work, named owners, latest start/finish dates and explicit fallback outcomes. Preserve the accepted 30 October profile milestone, but distinguish formal/profile exit from implemented evidence. If the critical path misses, apply the already stated cut-or-stop rule. Move design-batch housekeeping off that path. Do not add new integrated models, full LTV or original product gates merely to answer this review.
docs/reviews/v1-derivation/CODEX-REVIEW.md:238:**Exact fix:** List the actual V1 dependency/assumption manifest with exact algorithms, formats, trust configuration and historical-time interpretation. Say no renewal/standing service is offered by this profile, while independent custodians may preserve or renew its bytes under later protocols. Require later wrapper support to preserve the inner V1 assessment under identical declared inputs and report outer/LTV assessments separately. Do not present that future implementation property as already checked. State the shelf-life dependency plainly without making delivery of T4 a hidden V1 condition.
docs/reviews/v1-derivation/CODEX-REVIEW.md:248:**Exact fix:** Keep the explicit non-claims and status vocabulary. Date the DNS observation. Replace the present-tense delivery assessment with “V1 would demonstrate these checks if the listed formal/profile evidence and implemented acceptance tests pass.” Describe `UNVERIFIABLE` as an incomplete overall claim with useful scoped check results. Make the verdict and documentation identify the offered profile, evaluated dimensions, omitted dimensions, temporal semantics and assumptions directly. No liability hedge is needed: state exactly which facts the artifacts establish and which have not been tested.
