docs/reviews/amendment-9/DISPOSITION.md:12:| 1 | WORDING, adopted. The token stops key export, not misuse. Whoever controls the queue (an AWS takeover) has signing capability for both slots. "Signing capability for every required slot" is used throughout. MECHANISM, small: the token-side signer refuses a declared time outside ε of its own clock. That limits a takeover to current-time minting. Separation of control stays a V2 driver. |
docs/reviews/amendment-9/DISPOSITION.md:13:| 2, 10, 12 | MECHANISM. **A single issuance window for V1 of at most 90 days.** The registered invariant is `issuance-not-after − issuance-not-before ≤ 90 days`, so not-before becomes mandatory. No overlap. Before the window ends, either a rotation mechanism is registered (multiple records or per-key owner names) or issuance stops. Operating numbers (the retirement margin, a 30-day cadence) leave the instrument and go to the operations runbook. The retirement rule stays only as an invariant: an attempt whose T would exceed not-after is not shipped. |
