docs/reviews/profile-2026-10-19/CODEX-REVIEW.md:51:R5 says fingerprints arriving with releases authenticate nothing, but rotation authenticates the successor through a release. R3 refers only to the production key obtained through R5. Finally, recovery permits a replacement bootstrap, whereas §5 says a new release key is introduced *only* by the current key ([line 422](/home/tony/projects/tessera/docs/V1-PROFILE.md:422)).
