docs/reviews/profile-2026-10-19/CODEX-REVIEW.md:73:“A substituted or non-verifying signature that is present gives INVALID” follows a discussion including `possession.<slot>`. But another valid possession signature over the same manifest can pass: those signature bytes are not committed by `A_sig`. The profile explicitly recognizes possession-signature malleation at [line 1160](/home/tony/projects/tessera/docs/V1-PROFILE.md:1160). Unsupported algorithms also make signature semantics unperformable, rather than necessarily invalid ([line 1050](/home/tony/projects/tessera/docs/V1-PROFILE.md:1050)).
