docs/reviews/v1-profile-r2/CODEX-REVIEW.md:245:| G36 | §0.1, §5 | Matches custody as operating fact; repository root is distinct from release key. |
docs/reviews/v1-profile-r2/CODEX-REVIEW.md:260:| G27 half-range/reversed/equal | Sound as explicit owner edge policy: half-range has no unique nearest lift; resolved inception > expiration cannot contain T_snap; equal endpoints describe a one-second inclusive window. It does not prove support for every long DNSSEC interval or remove the need to aggregate edge reasons. Time is historical T_snap, not wall clock. [RFC 1982 comparison](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc1982.html#section-3.2). |
