docs/reviews/v1-profile-r2/CODEX-REVIEW.md:268:| A9 C5 versus E §7.1 “earliest” | A9's revised lowest-height reading governs. P implements it correctly. Change E's exact selection sentence, not only its publication/pre-commitment explanation, in §14.2 item 9. |
docs/reviews/v1-profile-r2/CODEX-REVIEW.md:272:| A9.5 full git path / E:685 “commit adds blob” versus P:971 | A9 requires authenticated path linkage, not proof of introduction. P's no-introduction check is reasonable, but E's “adds” overstates what is checked. Replace it with “whose tree contains the assertion blob at the profile path.” Add this to pending E edits. |
docs/reviews/v1-profile-r2/CODEX-REVIEW.md:273:| E §8 single in-profile byte UNVERIFIABLE | P:178–179 repeats the stale statement although P now adds missing-member/spec/form cases. Qualify it as **codec-level**, as G01 already requires in E. It is not a reason to turn those adopted cases INVALID. |
docs/reviews/v1-profile-r2/CODEX-REVIEW.md:274:| E rule O says codec ignores contents versus P G11 | A profile policy above the codec is permitted and labelled new; this alone is not a contradiction. Do not retrofit policy into codec vectors or infer generic keyring behavior. |
docs/reviews/v1-profile-r2/CODEX-REVIEW.md:289:5. **Amend item 8:** withdraw/replace L-27/L-28 and the obsolete clock code; add the distinguishing cases named in F01–F14. Referencing the old L list as a whole is insufficient.
docs/reviews/v1-profile-r2/CODEX-REVIEW.md:297:Release independence is load-bearing under the channel-capture adversary; the author must be told if it cannot be supplied. Ordinary evidence-format completion, reason ordering and the source corrections above can be decided by the owner within the stated profile scope, with change accounting. The three-document claim should then be stated as “sufficient with the frozen catalog, authenticated trust configuration and pinned normative dependencies,” rather than implying those external immutable inputs have disappeared.
docs/reviews/v1-profile-r2/CODEX-REVIEW.md:301:- Fresh read-only run: `PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 python3 formal/p8/vectors/check.py` returned **71/71 golden round-trips, 173/173 same-code rejections and 5/5 negative controls**. This validates the current P8 codec suite, not the new full profile or the proposed fixes.
docs/reviews/v1-profile-r2/CODEX-REVIEW.md:303:- Primary sources were checked for RFC 9580 subpacket/issuer semantics, RFC 4035 validation preconditions, RFC 1982 half-range comparison, Bitcoin transaction framing and IANA/ICANN KSK-2017 timing. A GitHub fetch for the OTS reader source failed; the profile's inline grammar, not that unavailable page, is the review basis. No new claim is made about today's corpus counts or calendar output stability.
