   357	## 4. Issue order (issuer side, binding on the build)
   358	
   359	1. Fix the manifest and common metadata, including `declared_issue_time`.
   360	2. Build both frames.
   361	3. Sign each frame.
   362	4. Verify both signatures with the exact bytes to be committed.
   363	5. Freeze the signature bytes. Any re-framing happens before this point.
   364	6. Build `A_sig` and stamp its SHA-256. One stamp per receipt.
   365	7. Obtain and validate the confirmation and time evidence.
   366	8. Ship the complete receipt.
   367	
   368	[ENC §5.4:515-525; A9:293-296] That is eight steps in both sources. A retry that changes any committed byte needs a
   369	fresh stamp. The frame-only anchor is withdrawn, with no fallback. [A9:292; ENC §5.1:407-414]
