   694	**Stages**, for each of the receipt, snapshot and git proofs:
   695	1. **Header pool.** Every supplied header, used or not, is checked against the pins. A header at a height with no
   696	   pin gives `UNVERIFIABLE / HEADERS_NOT_COVERED`; a header that differs from its pin gives `INVALID /
   697	   HEADER_CONFLICTS_PIN`.
   698	2. **Qualification ("verified").** A Bitcoin attestation at height h qualifies only if the bundled header at h has
   699	   a merkle root equal to the attestation message, headers h … h+5 are all bundled, each equals its pin, and each
   700	   links to the one before. Pin coverage is part of "verified". A pinned header at h whose merkle root contradicts
   701	   the attestation gives `INVALID / OTS_MERKLE_MISMATCH`.
   702	3. **Selection.** The selected anchor is the qualifying attestation at the lowest height h*. T and the confirmation
   703	   count come from h*. A non-qualifying attestation, including one without headers or one beyond the newest pin,
   704	   is never selected; it supplies no fact and is not a failed check, except as stages 1–2 state. A failed check at
